-- boolean operators: && / || lower to short-circuiting CIf, comparisons yield
-- Bool words.  Result is a Bool -> mdk_print_bool.
-- Was `!(a == b)` until #1739 half A repurposed `!` to Ref-deref: there is no
-- unary BOOLEAN operator any more (and so no xor lowering to pin), and `not` is
-- a prelude FUNCTION this no-prelude emit driver cannot resolve.  `/=` keeps the
-- negated-comparison operand without leaving the fixture's driver.
a = 5
b = 9
main = (a < b) && (a /= b) || (a > b)
